d/VpnHood/commit/4550599c92018d732f8191e41309b7c1160df316","commit_subject":"Windows VPN plug-in: the app talks to the VPN host through the package's app service, and the VPN works without the app - Windows freezes the host between VPN events, so the named pipe's requests waited for the next one; the app service runs in the host's own process and keeps it running while a full-trust process holds it, the app's (WindowsVpnPluginAppServiceClient, ...Listener, VpnAppServiceTask) or the host's own executable, which it starts with full trust after each connect (WindowsVpnPluginKeepAwake, the manifest's second app service and windows.fullTrustProcess) and again if it goes; the service ends a connection itself through Windows (StopSelf asks Windows to disconnect the profile, and Windows' Disconnect stops the channel, never the adapter), as a channel the plug-in stops is a dropped one that Windows dials again; a connect the server refuses ends at once with its reason, where it held Windows' Connect 60 s and showed Windows' bare status; the pipe's client and listener deleted","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"sanity-io/sanity-astro","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:44Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"47c6613eab88251231a30cd988c28a7decc19287","github_link":"https://github.com/sanity-io/sanity-astro/commit/47c6613eab88251231a30cd988c28a7decc19287","commit_subject":"feat: infer types from branded .groq queries (#514)","ai_tool":"Cursor"},{"repo_name":"dotnet/diagnostics","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:34Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"37580df5a32332c90962f7b003a7625cac93744d","github_link":"https://github.com/dotnet/diagnostics/commit/37580df5a32332c90962f7b003a7625cac93744d","commit_subject":"Add automated cDAC source synchronization (#6127)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"carapace-sh/carapace-bin","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:10Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"c33976561dbb688439a343e931f58f5bdee4eb7b","github_link":"https://github.com/carapace-sh/carapa